<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#bandIndex> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for logical raster samples, bands and arrays after parsing. Logical dimensions are independent of physical DLV addressing; partial graphs and complete dimension lists have different completeness contracts. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#coordinateArray> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Array of coordinate values associated with a dimension. Its shape and alignment are asserted by the profile; coordinates need not be regularly spaced."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#coordinateArray> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for logical raster samples, bands and arrays after parsing. Logical dimensions are independent of physical DLV addressing; partial graphs and complete dimension lists have different completeness contracts. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#dimensionExtent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Current number of indexable values along this logical axis. Zero is permitted. An unlimited dimension has a finite current extent, not infinity."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#dimensionExtent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for logical raster samples, bands and arrays after parsing. Logical dimensions are independent of physical DLV addressing; partial graphs and complete dimension lists have different completeness contracts. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#dimensionKind> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Axis nature from a profile-bound concept scheme; no fixed list limits scientific or non-spatial axes."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#dimensionKind> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for logical raster samples, bands and arrays after parsing. Logical dimensions are independent of physical DLV addressing; partial graphs and complete dimension lists have different completeness contracts. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#dimensionName> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The source-level name of a logical array dimension, independent of its position in any one array."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#dimensionName> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for logical raster samples, bands and arrays after parsing. Logical dimensions are independent of physical DLV addressing; partial graphs and complete dimension lists have different completeness contracts. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#dimensions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Complete ordered RDF list of ArrayDimension resources in logical indexing order. rdf:nil denotes a scalar. The list must be finite, well formed and permit repeated dimension resources at distinct positions."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#dimensions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for logical raster samples, bands and arrays after parsing. Logical dimensions are independent of physical DLV addressing; partial graphs and complete dimension lists have different completeness contracts. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#hasArray> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A logical array contained in a group, independent of its physical storage path."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#hasArray> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for logical raster samples, bands and arrays after parsing. Logical dimensions are independent of physical DLV addressing; partial graphs and complete dimension lists have different completeness contracts. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#hasBand> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A band view belonging to a raster grid. A reused physical sample plane may need distinct band views when its position differs between grids."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#hasBand> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for logical raster samples, bands and arrays after parsing. Logical dimensions are independent of physical DLV addressing; partial graphs and complete dimension lists have different completeness contracts. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#hasGroup> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A logical child group within an acyclic array-group hierarchy."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#hasGroup> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for logical raster samples, bands and arrays after parsing. Logical dimensions are independent of physical DLV addressing; partial graphs and complete dimension lists have different completeness contracts. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#hasMask> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Validity mask band: zero is invalid; nonzero is valid. This relation does not imply alpha/transparency semantics."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#hasMask> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for logical raster samples, bands and arrays after parsing. Logical dimensions are independent of physical DLV addressing; partial graphs and complete dimension lists have different completeness contracts. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#hasOverview> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A lower-resolution representation covering the same logical domain. Does not assert a resampling algorithm or an integer reduction factor."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#hasOverview> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for logical raster samples, bands and arrays after parsing. Logical dimensions are independent of physical DLV addressing; partial graphs and complete dimension lists have different completeness contracts. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#height> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Grid extent along the vertical axis, in samples (pixels)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#height> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for logical raster samples, bands and arrays after parsing. Logical dimensions are independent of physical DLV addressing; partial graphs and complete dimension lists have different completeness contracts. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#noDataValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Sample value denoting absence of data in the grid."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#noDataValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for logical raster samples, bands and arrays after parsing. Logical dimensions are independent of physical DLV addressing; partial graphs and complete dimension lists have different completeness contracts. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#sampleOffset> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Calibration additive term, in the unit of the physical value. Independent of byte offsets and georeferencing origins."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#sampleOffset> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for logical raster samples, bands and arrays after parsing. Logical dimensions are independent of physical DLV addressing; partial graphs and complete dimension lists have different completeness contracts. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#sampleScale> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Calibration multiplier: physical = raw * sampleScale + sampleOffset. Absence means unspecified, not a stored default. Apply no-data detection to raw samples first."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#sampleScale> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for logical raster samples, bands and arrays after parsing. Logical dimensions are independent of physical DLV addressing; partial graphs and complete dimension lists have different completeness contracts. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#sampleUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Unit IRI for calibrated sample values; profiles may reuse established unit vocabularies."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#sampleUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for logical raster samples, bands and arrays after parsing. Logical dimensions are independent of physical DLV addressing; partial graphs and complete dimension lists have different completeness contracts. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#width> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Grid extent along the horizontal axis, in samples (pixels)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#width> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for logical raster samples, bands and arrays after parsing. Logical dimensions are independent of physical DLV addressing; partial graphs and complete dimension lists have different completeness contracts. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
